Z||000004||Alex4mula||09-17-2001||08:43 AM||||Very nice car! Are those Jacobs wires? What you did to stick those 17x9 in the back? Coil overs?||||reg||1
Z||000005||MinnGreenGT||09-17-2001||10:33 AM||||Nice pics... where/who did you get your wood dash kit from?  looks nice!  I also like the painted underside of the decklid.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/halfpole.gif">  <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000006||88CoupeV6||09-17-2001||10:35 AM||||Where did you get that Polished stainless panel that you have on your decklid? Ive been looking for some everywhere.  Thanks, Car looks Great  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">   <BR><B>Also 88 Yellow GT</B> :D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||5
Z||000007||LT1 Chop Top||09-17-2001||04:58 PM||||Alex4mula,<P>The whole system is Jacobs: Energy Team Ignition, and 'Ultra Coil' ignition coil.<P>MinnGreen,<P>The dash is from Dennis Lagura...he used to sell them off his website, I was lucky to get one of his last kits.  I think he only sells turbos now.<BR>I like the painted underside too, it was a mod done by the previous owner, I recently applied it to the Great Blue Chop Top also....what an improvement!<P>88CoupeV6,<P>The panel under the deck lid is a mirror that I had cut to fit at a glass shop.  I had to cut a pattern out of cardboard, and they cut it EXACTLY to the pattern.  I used 6 velcro squares to hold it in place, as I don't want to drive with glass over the belts!  Total cost was $18.  I got many compliments on that at the show.||||reg||14
Z||000008||jelly2m8||09-17-2001||10:27 PM||||Nice pics of both your cars! SWEET!!!<P>I like the Pontiac Emblem on the front fascia, nice effect.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Nashco||09-17-2001||11:04 PM||||Hey, sweet ride!  Would you mind giving us a little info on your wheels?  What width/offset are they?  I'm in the market for some wheels, and I'm trying to get a feel for the size options available on my 88.  Thanks for any help!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000010||LT1 Chop Top||09-17-2001||11:20 PM||||Nashco,<P>I unfortunately do not know the offset of the wheels.  They are DP Enduro 3 piece 17x9 rear, and 16x7.5 front.  They were special order from the factory in Japan, and as far as I know, the only other set that was made for Fiero were once on my car, but were all 16", they were sold when the previous owner bought these.||||reg||2
Z||000011||Urchin||09-17-2001||11:39 PM||||Beautiful car.  A few questions.<BR>1.  What is the Pontiac emblem on the nose off of?<BR>2.  Do you have any pictures of the front trunk compartment (ie. spare tire)?<BR>3.  What colour is that (custom mix)?<BR>4.  Where are the side scoops from?<P>Thanks..<P><BR>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/final.jpg">  <BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.<p>[This message has been edited by Urchin (edited 09-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||Urchin||09-18-2001||07:32 PM||||..||||reg||1
Z||000013||LT1 Chop Top||09-19-2001||05:27 PM||||Urchin,<P>1. Emblem was from the dealer (picked from several avail.)<P>2. Unfortunately I don't have any pics of the front compartment (took 75 pics...and none of that part of either car..DOH!)  It is exceptionally clean, and is finished off with a Dickman spare tire cover.<P>3. The paint is factory metallic red w/ additional pearl added.<P>4. Side scoops are actually factory prototype, that were left over from early production.  They were discontinued as the edges tend to get tiny rock chips.  The pervious owner had a connection to the inside.  The scoops on my friends 87 White GT (see San Antonio show thread) were made from molds that were cast from another set of prototype scoops identical to mine.  They look/fit the same, but the prototype are much higher quality.  I think you can get them from Fiero Motorsports.||||reg||14
